      "description": "Watch Al Faisaly FC vs Neom SC highlights and goals from Pro League - Saudi Arabia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 21, 2026. Lacazette Double Seals Al Faisaly Victory Over Neom SC Alexandre Lacazette was the star of the show, netting twice to guide Al Faisaly FC to a crucial 2-0 victory against Neom SC in a hard-fought Pro League encounter on August 21, 2026 . The match was a testament to the league's competitive nature, with key moments shaping the final outcome. First Half a Tactical Battle The opening period saw a cautious approach from both sides. An early substitution for Al Faisaly in the 6th minute saw Haroune Camara replace Said Benrahma , suggesting an immediate tactical adjustment. Neom SC also made an enforced change in the 27th minute, with Ayman Fallatah coming on for Abdullah Al-Mogren . The midfield battle was intense, leading to several fouls and a yellow card for Theo Bongonda in the 37th minute. Second Half Spark and Decisive Goals The second half witnessed a significant shift in tempo. Just 51 minutes into the match, Al Faisaly broke the deadlock. Khalil Al Absi provided the assist for Alexandre Lacazette , who found the back of the net to give his side the lead. The celebrations were somewhat tempered as Christian Bassogog received a yellow card in the 56th minute. However, Al Faisaly's attacking prowess shone through again in the 59th minute. Haroune Camara turned provider, setting up Lacazette for his second goal of the game, doubling Al Faisaly's advantage. With a commanding lead, Al Faisaly focused on controlling the game, while Neom SC continued to push for a way back into the match. Both teams made several substitutions throughout the second half to inject fresh energy, with Neom SC making changes in the 73rd, 79th, and 82nd minutes, and Al Faisaly following suit in the 79th and 82nd minutes. Despite late efforts from Neom SC , Al Faisaly held firm. After five minutes of added time, and with Neom SC making a final substitution in the 90+1 minute, bringing on Khalifah Al-Dawsari for Khalil Al Absi , the referee blew the final whistle, confirming Al Faisaly FC's victory."
