      "description": "Watch Al Hilal Saudi FC vs Al Faisaly FC highlights and goals from Pro League - Saudi Arabia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 14, 2026. The Saudi Pro League atmosphere was electric as two competitive sides clashed on a high-stakes night. Fans were treated to a rollercoaster encounter where momentum shifted dramatically between the heavyweights and their determined opponents. Dominant Start for the Hosts The match on August 14, 2026 , began with Al Hilal Saudi FC asserting their authority early in this fixture. The breakthrough came in the 19th minute when Karim Benzema stepped up to the spot, coolly converting a penalty to ignite the home crowd. The pressure didn't stop there; just seven minutes later, Malcom doubled the lead with a clinical finish, leaving Al Faisaly FC reeling. Before the half-hour mark, the referee awarded another penalty, which Ruben Neves hammered home in the 29th minute to establish a commanding three-goal cushion heading into the break. Al Faisaly’s Spirited Response The second half saw a completely different energy from Al Faisaly . Refusing to go down without a fight, they began to exploit gaps in the Al Hilal defense. In the 58th minute, Alexandre Mendy pulled one back following a precise assist from Jaime Seoane . The momentum shifted further in the 64th minute when Theo Bongonda found the net, assisted by Christian Bassogog , cutting the deficit to just one goal. The tension in the stadium was palpable as the visitors pushed for an equalizer, while Abdullah Al-Mogren picked up a yellow card in the heat of the battle. Neves Seals the Result With the game hanging in the balance, Al Hilal managed to regain their composure. In the 82nd minute, they were awarded their third penalty of the match. Ruben Neves stepped up once again and made no mistake, scoring his second goal of the night to provide much-needed breathing room. A flurry of substitutions followed, including Nasser Al-Dawsari and Sultan Mandash coming on to see out the game. Despite five minutes of added time, Al Hilal held firm to secure the points in a thrilling encounter."
